BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-koronos-argokoili-pilgrimage-of-panagia-argokoiliotissa-koro-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270506
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270508
SUMMARY:Pilgrimage of Panagia Argokoiliotissa\, Koronos
LOCATION:Koronos (Argokoili)\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the Friday of Bright Week (five days after Easter) the whole of Naxos climbs to Argokoili above Koronos\, where the icon of the Virgin was found in 1836: the icon is carried down from the old church on Thursday evening and back up with a huge procession around 10:30 on Friday morning\, with the Metropolitan\, a vigil overnight and stalls selling food. Many walk up from Koronos\; if you drive\, park early on the road below because it fills for kilometres.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#koronos-argokoili-pilgrimage-of-panagia-argokoiliotissa-koro
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#koronos-argokoili-pilgrimage-of-panagia-argokoiliotissa-koro
END:VEVENT
