BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-kinidaros-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kinidaros-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Kinidaros
LOCATION:Kinidaros\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kinidaros\, the marble-quarry village famous for having the most tavernas per head on Naxos\, feasts Agia Paraskevi on the evening of 25 July with grilled meat\, wine and raki and violins in the square. The village also celebrates the Holy Cross on 14 September and Agios Nikolaos on 6 December in the same style.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#kinidaros-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kinidaros
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#kinidaros-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kinidaros
