DESCRIPTION:Apeiranthos\, the marble-paved village with Cretan roots\, does its own Dormition feast on 14-15 August with the village's celebrated violin players\, kotsakia (improvised rhyming couplets)\, local wine and food in the square\, competing with Filoti a few kilometres away. If you want a slightly smaller crowd and the best musicians\, this is the one.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#apeiranthos-dormition-panigiri-apeiranthos
